    "created_at": "2019-10-05T09:25:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-05T09:25:15Z",
    "body": "> ... is there any way the status could be computed in the background, cached, and the prompt would just show the most recent cached value?\r\n\r\nYes, but not given our current architecture. Something of the sort would require a daemon to run in the background to passively update the data available to the prompt, which we are considering for future versions of the prompt.\r\n\r\nAs it stands, caching would be possible, but that would still require a long initial prompt render. We may need to look into alternate ways to do these checks.",
